   "source": [
    "What's happening: Your courier (requests) goes to https://example.com, knocks on the server's door, and says, \"Hey, can I have the HTML code for this page?\" * The server hands it over, and you store that entire digital package inside a variable called page.\n",
    "What's happening: You take the raw HTML text (page.text) and hand it to BeautifulSoup.\n",
    "\n",
    "The \"html.parser\" part is just telling Python: \"Hey, treat this like standard website code, map out the structure, and make it searchable.\" Now, the variable soup holds a neatly organized version of the website.\n",
    "What's happening: You are telling your organized soup: \"Find the HTML element called <title>, and just give me the plain human text inside it.\"\n",
    "\n",
    "If the website's code looks like <title>Example Domain</title>, this line will simply print: Example Domain."
   ]
